 by accelerating capitalism  which some socialists believe will fail  some marxist some communists believe  will fail you  accelerate the eventual revolution  that will turn the country socialistic  much has been said theoretically about  that and written theoretically about  that i believe that in practice  at this point in time again in five  years maybe i'd have a different view  because things dramatically change  right now i don't see how for example  giving trump another four years and  cutting regulations and giving more  market power  i don't think that if that causes a  breakdown  it results in the united states becoming  socialist  if and and so this is why i've said time  and again to actual socialists of which  there are relatively few in the united  states  many of the people who even think they  are socialists aren't really socialists  up for now you should just be joining  the fight for social democracy because  the path or let me put it a different  way  the best proof that you the united  states should go in that direction  would be to go in that direction and  that would mean  uh looking at healthcare more like  northern european countries  look at it looking at taxation more the  way northern european countries look at  it look at education  social welfare programs etc  in the last decade we have seen  socialist go from really more of an  insult and not something many people  would use to describe themselves  to kind of like a pretty ho-hum you know  it's just a word it's almost become  like progressive although it means very  different things where trump says all  his opponents are socialists very few  people really believe it  young people are more okay with the term  than we've seen people be in a very long  time so i think that  and it's not for me to give advice to  the actual socialists not being one but  if you are an  actual socialist you should capitalize  on  the most positive or least negative view  of socialism that there's been in the us  in a long time  by pushing the country in any ways that  are possible in that direction  the best argument you can make for  socialism being great  would be for social democracy to work  really well  and if we ever got to that point then i  and the socialists would be on different  sides  uh but but right now even though many of  the socialists  believe they're on a different side than  me the next step whether you want social  democracy as the end point or you want  socialism as the end point  would be to move in that direction when  it comes to all of the major  uh areas of policy in the united states  it's certainly not going to happen with  another four years of donald trump
 

